- action(n1, "start screening process"): Hallucinates a preliminary step; the source explicitly states the process "begins by reviewing the support request", with no preceding action documented.
- action(n4, "end procedure"): Hallucinates a terminal step; the source states the process "comes to an end" immediately after communicating with the customer, which is already semantically complete with the `end(e1)` node.
- actor(a_default, "Default", [...]): Misrepresents responsibilities; the source attributes the workflow to "screening staff", whereas the model assigns all nodes to an unspecified "Default" actor.